---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Legacy archive status — IFL PvP MegaGuides';
const description = 'A transparent status page for restored MegaGuides and legacy IFL PvP material that remains in the private archive.';
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} canonicalPath="/archive/" noindex>
  <section class="page-hero" aria-labelledby="archive-title">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legacy archive</p>
      <h1 id="archive-title">Five complete guide bodies restored. The wider archive stays protected.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede">The detailed Battlerite, Bloodline Champions, Gigantic, GunZ, and Marvel Rivals references are public again. The remaining legacy archive stays private until individual routes pass rights and evidence review.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What came back</h2>
      <p>The five established MegaGuide routes now contain their authored mechanics, roster, ability, strategy, history, and reference tables. Publisher media was removed and each edition is clearly labeled as historical or patch-specific.</p>
      <h2>Why the rest is not a bulk import</h2>
      <p>Historical writing can be useful, but it should not be mistaken for current, supported game advice. Older pages may also include media, datasets, or source claims that are not cleared for this public repository.</p>
      <h2>What a restored route needs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>a documented right to publish the text and any included assets;</li>
        <li>primary sources for material factual claims, with checked dates;</li>
        <li>a clear historical or current scope statement; and</li>
        <li>a visible review and indexing decision.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you are looking for another previously published page, please use the restored guide routes or send a request through the correction process. A missing page is not represented as a current public source.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
